Think: Normalize PATH entries by trimming whitespace, expanding ~ to $HOME, and removing trailing slashes (but preserve root '/') and save to temp_workspace/normalized_entries.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -v HOME="$HOME" '{
  line=$0;
  gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/,"",line);
  if(line=="~") line=HOME;
  else if(line ~ /^~\//) sub(/^~/, HOME, line);
  if(line != "/" && length(line)>1) sub(/\/+$/,"",line);
  print line
}' temp_workspace/path_entries.txt > temp_workspace/normalized_entries.txt
```

