Think: Interpret the raw var value into a canonical numeric form (or record failure) and save it to int_check_workspace/var_numeric.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  s=(NR==1?$0: s "\n" $0)
}
END{
  # trim
  gsub(/^[ \t\r\n]+|[ \t\r\n]+$/,"",s)
  if(s==""){ print "ERROR: empty"; exit }
  if(s ~ /^[-+]?[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?([eE][-+]?[0-9]+)?$/){
    # normalize numeric representation
    printf "%.16g\n", (s + 0)
  } else {
    print "ERROR: not a number: " s
  }
}' int_check_workspace/var_raw.txt > int_check_workspace/var_numeric.txt
